    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **294 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `namesakeCount` feature: when an owner is created, the count of other owners already sharing the same last name is computed and returned in the owner response.\n\nChanges (following the existing pattern used for `membershipNumber`, `customerCode`, `membershipTier`):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer property (min 0) to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient` `namesakeCount` field with getter/setter (transient because the value is a snapshot computed at creation time, not persisted state). MapStruct picks it up automatically by name.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, added `owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner.getLastName()))` before persisting, plus a `countNamesakes` helper that counts existing owners with a matching last name. It reuses the existing `normalize(...)` helper (case- and whitespace-insensitive), consistent with the city/email duplicate checks in this class, and is evaluated before the new owner is saved so the new owner never counts itself.\n\n4. **Tests** \u2014 Added two tests: one for a shared last name (two seed \"Davis\" owners \u2192 `namesakeCount` = 2) and one for a unique last name (`namesakeCount` = 0).",
